<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Enhancement Shaman Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>For trinkets, Enhancement Shamans aim for Agility, Mastery, Haste, or Critical Strike. Generally, two passive Real Procs per Minute (RPPM) trinkets are preferred if possible. RPPM trinkets were added in Mists of Pandaria and have an average amount of procs per minute assigned to them. It is capable of proccing more then the stated amount, but should average out.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94511/vicious-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_speedoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> plays very well into the burst heavy playstyle of Enhancement Shamans. This is the strongest in fights that are shorter than 180 seconds, or where mechanics will naturaly disconnect and reconnect you from the boss when your cooldowns align.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96369/renatakis-soul-charm">
<img alt="Renataki's Soul Charm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Renataki's Soul Charm</span></a> offers a lot of static Expertise, which can free up some secondary stats in reforges and the stacking Agility proc offers some unique snapshot opportunities for strong Flame Shocks.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96409/bad-juju">
<img alt="Bad Juju" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_troll_voodoodoll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bad Juju</span></a> provides a lot of Mastery and a strong Agility proc. The additional damage from the Voodoo Gnomes is not impactful.</div></li></ul>
