<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the  <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. For the vast majority of Raid bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry from behind. Expertise will also add to your Spell Hit. By reaching 7.5% in both Expertise and Hit, you will be able to reach 15% Spell Hit.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>You will try your best to match the sockets gem color whenever possible. The main goal is to stack Agility through your gems, but the extra Hit or Expertise allows for more optimal gearing and reforging. Avoid gemming pure Hit or Expertise, except for Engineering gems. However, if your gear won't allow you to reach your caps, try to gem the rest of the way, trying to match socket colors.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76692/delicate-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76670/adept-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Adept Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Adept Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76680/glinting-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Glinting Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glinting Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="r2">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>Mists of Pandaria has balanced profession bonuses quite well, but some offer unique advantages for Enhancement Shamans.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/trade_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Enhancement Shamans</h4>Remains the best profession for raiding in Mists of Pandaria as well. The value of the tinkers like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126392/goblin-glider">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Goblin Glider</span></a> is immense and should be considered carefully by everyone interested in raiding at any level.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="alchemy">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_alchemy.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Alchemy for Enhancement Shamans</h4>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a> is a strong early choice thanks to the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> trinket. It is a pre-raid BiS item due to its high stat value. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=53042/mixology">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_112.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mixology</span></a> increases the duration and effectiveness of our Flasks. A great bonus is being able to craft all of your Flasks and Pots yourself, making raiding just a bit cheaper to maintain.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="herbalism">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_herbalism.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Herbalism for Enhancement Shamans</h4>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=182/herbalism">
<img alt="Herbalism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_herbalism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Herbalism</span></a> is good to prepare early since it is seeing its use in raiding for the first time. It provides us with the on-use Haste cooldown <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=121279/lifeblood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_wispsplodegreen.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifeblood</span></a>, which we can use to even further increase our strong burst. It can also be used to generate some Gold through farming and selling Herbs for others to use.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Enhancement Shamans</h4>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=197/tailoring">
<img alt="Tailoring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_tailoring.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tailoring</span></a> provides us with a strong Cloak Enchant <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125483/swordguard-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swordguard Embroidery</span></a>,  which will play well into our burst heavy damage profile. The gear crafted from Tailoring will unfortunately not be usable as an Enhancement Shaman, but we can still use this to help out friends or guildmates, or sell crafts for profit.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Enhancement Shamans</span></h3>Leatherworking in Phase 3 provides 2 new Mail items with 522 item level. The Helmet <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94272/dreadrunner-helm">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Helm</span></a> and the Boots <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94271/dreadrunner-sabatons">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Sabatons" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Sabatons</span></a>, which nearly rival heroic raid boots from Throne of Thunder. The Helmet can be a great offpiece until you get your T15 gear and the Boots are close to the Heroic Raid Boots, so they should be considered pre-BiS.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
